**[Question 5] - What are the key components of my approach and results?**

Our approach will leverage the AdaFire SNN model, known for its efficient spiking dynamics, and utilize ComplEx KGEs, which are well-suited for representing relational data. We will implement a novel architecture where the ComplEx embeddings are used to modulate the spiking activity of the AdaFire neurons, effectively encoding item and user relationships within the SNN. The retrieval stage will consist of a shallow AdaFire network trained to classify candidate items based on their KGE representation. The ranking stage will utilize a deeper AdaFire network, incorporating attention mechanisms to weigh the influence of different KGE features. We will evaluate the system using Recall@K (e.g., Recall@10 and Recall@20) and NDCG@K (e.g., NDCG@10 and NDCG@20) as primary metrics.  Latency and energy consumption will also be measured to quantify the energy efficiency gains. We will train and evaluate our system on the MovieLens-1M dataset, a widely used benchmark for recommendation systems. We expect to demonstrate a significant improvement in retrieval efficiency (reduced latency) and a comparable or improved ranking accuracy compared to baseline multi-stage cascade systems, while maintaining a lower energy footprint."}
